Z||000000||Shiner||05-22-2000||10:51 PM||||I just thought I would tell you that I don't have a cat converter on my car.  The reason? Well, the 454 Chevy big block V8 in my fiero doesn't like to run with a cat.  It likes a straight exhaust better (even though 15 Perigrine Falcons dropped dead just from the noise)  It's supercharged, so it gets about 5mpg, but it's not gas, it's alchohol.  For all this power, I need to run slicks so it can hook up on that horrible street pavement around here.  I have to adjust the carb too, because on downshifts, it seems to be dumping raw alcohol down, sending 8ft flames from the tail pipes (which singed the fur of no less than 26 neighborhood dogs, whom I then put out of their misery with the H&K MP5 I carry in my car without a class 3 weapons permit)  My next project?  I am putting a military surplus F-14 Tomcat turbine engine in Vista Cruiser, so I can get those illegal aliens and cocaine across the border before the police can catch me.  ||||reg||1
